== X Æ A-Xii Musk ==
[[File:Elon Musk and X Æ A-Xii in Oval Office (February 2025).jpg|thumb|X Æ A-Xii Musk in February 2025]]
X Æ A-Xii Musk ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|ɛ|k|s|_|eɪ|.|aɪ|_|eɪ|_|t|w|ɛ|l|v}} or {{IPAc-en|ˈ|ɛ|k|s|_|æ|ʃ|_|eɪ|_|t|w|ɛ|l|v}}<ref>{{Cite news |last=Harrison |first=Ellie |date=12 February 2025 |title=X Æ A-Xii: How to pronounce the name of Elon Musk and Grimes' son |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/news/elon-musk-child-name-grimes-pronounce-x-ae-a-xii-b2696911.html |access-date=March 22, 2025 |work=[[The Independent]]}}</ref>) was born in May 2020, the eldest child of Elon Musk and Grimes.<ref name="Kiefer-2020" /><ref name="Trepany-2020" /> Musk and Grimes originally gave the baby the name "X [[Æ]] [[Lockheed A-12|A-12]]", which would have violated California regulations because it contained characters (Arabic numerals) that are not in the modern English alphabet.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Schwedel |first=Heather |date=May 5, 2020 |title=What Does Elon Musk and Grimes' Baby Name Actually Mean? |url=https://slate.com/human-interest/2020/05/elon-musk-grimes-baby-name.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200524150019/https://slate.com/human-interest/2020/05/elon-musk-grimes-baby-name.html |archive-date=May 24, 2020 |access-date=May 5, 2020 |work=Slate}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Lerman |first=Rachel |date=May 8, 2020 |title=Elon Musk's baby name isn't just weird, it may be against California regulations |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2020/05/08/musk-grimes-baby-name/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201231225820/https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2020/05/08/musk-grimes-baby-name/ |archive-date=December 31, 2020 |access-date=January 11, 2021 |work=The Washington Post}}</ref> They then changed it to "X Æ A-[[Roman numerals|Xii]]".<ref>{{Cite news |last=Guy |first=Jack |date=May 25, 2020 |title=Elon Musk and Grimes have changed their baby's name. A bit |url=https://www.cnn.com/2020/05/25/entertainment/grimes-musk-baby-name-tweak-scli-intl/index.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200525204407/https://www.cnn.com/2020/05/25/entertainment/grimes-musk-baby-name-tweak-scli-intl/index.html |archive-date=May 25, 2020 |access-date=May 25, 2020 |publisher=CNN}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Cooper |first=Gael Fashingbauer |date=June 16, 2020 |title=Elon Musk and Grimes saved a surprise for son X Æ A-12's birth certificate |url=https://www.cnet.com/news/elon-musk-and-grimes-saved-a-surprise-for-son-x-ae-a-12s-birth-certificate/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200617021513/https://www.cnet.com/news/elon-musk-and-grimes-saved-a-surprise-for-son-x-ae-a-12s-birth-certificate/ |archive-date=June 17, 2020 |access-date=June 17, 2020 |publisher=CNET}}</ref> They have received criticism for choosing a name perceived to be impractical and difficult to pronounce.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Elon Musk and Grimes' newborn name X Æ A-12 'fails at the basic job of being a name,' says author |url=https://www.cbc.ca/radio/thecurrent/the-current-for-may-7-2020-1.5559171/elon-musk-and-grimes-newborn-name-x-%C3%A6-a-12-fails-at-the-basic-job-of-being-a-name-says-author-1.5559761 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240812165748/https://www.cbc.ca/radio/thecurrent/the-current-for-may-7-2020-1.5559171/elon-musk-and-grimes-newborn-name-x-%C3%A6-a-12-fails-at-the-basic-job-of-being-a-name-says-author-1.5559761 |archive-date=August 12, 2024 |access-date=August 12, 2024 |publisher=CBC Radio}}</ref>

Elon Musk has taken X Æ A-Xii to multiple official events in Washington, D.C., during [[Second presidency of Donald Trump|Trump's second term in office]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chang |first=Emily |date=12 February 2025 |title=Musk's son 'Lil X' steals spotlight in the Oval Office |url=https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/musks-son-lil-steals-spotlight-oval-office/story?id=118713138 |access-date=15 February 2025 |website=ABC News}}</ref>

== Errol Musk ==
{{Main|Errol Musk}}
[[File:Errol Musk on Anything Goes With James English in 2025.png|thumb|150px|Errol Musk in 2025]]
Errol Graham Musk is a [[South Africa]]n politician and businessman,<ref name="Hull-2014">{{Cite web |last=Hull |first=Dana |last2=May |first2=Patrick |date=April 20, 2014 |title=Exploring the otherworldly ambitions of Elon Musk |url=https://buffalonews.com/business/local/exploring-the-otherworldly-ambitions-of-elon-musk/article_2fc57479-93eb-5016-b724-016b48a4f4f3.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220417231627/https://buffalonews.com/business/local/exploring-the-otherworldly-ambitions-of-elon-musk/article_2fc57479-93eb-5016-b724-016b48a4f4f3.html |archive-date=April 17, 2022 |access-date=July 15, 2022 |website=[[Buffalo News]]}}</ref> who was elected as an independent to represent [[Sunnyside, Pretoria|Sunnyside]] on the [[Pretoria]] City Council in 1972.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Eligon |first=John |last2=Chutel |first2=Lynsey |date=May 5, 2022 |title=Elon Musk Left a South Africa That Was Rife With Misinformation and White Privilege |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/05/world/africa/elon-musk-south-africa.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221111015804/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/05/world/africa/elon-musk-south-africa.html |archive-date=November 11, 2022 |access-date=September 6, 2023 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

Musk had a lucrative engineering business which took on "large projects such as office buildings, retail complexes, residential subdivisions, and an air force base." He also owned an auto parts store, at least half a share in an emerald mine, and even "one of the biggest houses in Pretoria".<ref name="Vance-2017">{{Cite book |last=Vance |first=Ashlee |author-link=Ashlee Vance |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ISBN9782212594379 |title=Elon Musk: Tesla, Paypal, SpaceX: l'entrepreneur qui va changer le monde |publisher=Eyrolles |year=2017 |isbn=9782212594379 |page=40 |language=fr}}{{Dead link|date=July 2024 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref><ref name="Friend-2009">{{Cite magazine |last=Friend |first=Tad |author-link=Tad Friend |date=August 17, 2009 |title=Plugged In - Can Elon Musk lead the way to an electric-car future? |url=http://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2009/08/24/plugged-in |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141010001525/http://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2009/08/24/plugged-in |archive-date=October 10, 2014 |access-date=June 28, 2024 |magazine=[[The New Yorker|New Yorker]] |pages=50–59 |volume=85 |issue=25}}</ref> He was married to [[Maye Musk]] from 1970 to 1979.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Holson |first=Laura M. |date=April 30, 2016 |title=At 68, Maye Musk, the Mother of Elon, Is Reclaiming the Spotlight |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/01/fashion/elon-musk-mother-maye-musk-model-met-gala.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200628120358/https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/01/fashion/elon-musk-mother-maye-musk-model-met-gala.html |archive-date=June 28, 2020 |access-date=July 15, 2022 |work=[[The New York Times]] |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref name="Friend-2009" />

Maye's book recalls that at the time of the divorce, he owned two homes, a yacht, a plane, five luxury cars, and a truck.<ref>{{Cite book |last=Musk |first=Maye |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=BDinDwAAQBAJ |title=A Woman Makes a Plan: Advice for a Lifetime of Adventure, Beauty, and Success |date=December 31, 2019 |publisher=Penguin |isbn=978-1-9848-7851-9 |via=Google Books}}</ref>

In the early 1990s, Errol, then aged 45, married Heide Bezuidenhout, a 25-year old he described as "one of the best looking women I've ever seen in my life".<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Mier |first=Tomás |date=July 14, 2022 |title=Like Father Like Son: Elon Musk's Dad Has Secret Second Kid With Stepdaughter |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/culture/culture-news/elon-musk-dad-has-secret-second-child-1383353/ |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref> They had two children.<ref name="Crilly-2018">{{Cite news |last=Crilly |first=Rob |author-link=Rob Crilly |date=March 25, 2018 |title=Elon Musk's father has baby with step-daughter he has known since she was four |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2018/03/25/elon-musks-father-has-baby-step-daughter-has-known-since-four/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210426231132/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2018/03/25/elon-musks-father-has-baby-step-daughter-has-known-since-four/ |archive-date=April 26, 2021 |access-date=July 15, 2022 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph|The Telegraph]] |issn=0307-1235}}</ref> Jana Bezuidenhout, who later became his romantic partner, was his stepdaughter from that marriage, four years old at the time Errol became her stepfather.<ref name="Crilly-2018" /><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Ball |first=Molly |last2=Kluger |first2=Jeffrey |last3=De la Garza |first3=Alejandro |date=December 13, 2021 |title=Elon Musk Is TIME's 2021 Person of the Year |url=https://time.com/person-of-the-year-2021-elon-musk/ |access-date=September 9, 2023 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]] |language=en}}</ref>

Errol Musk's mother, Cora Amelia Robinson, was English from [[Liverpool]], and his father, Walter Henry James Musk, was mostly English-South African.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Sommerlad |first=Joe |date=December 9, 2022 |title=Who are Elon Musk's relatives? |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/tech/elon-musk-family-maye-errol-b2241367.html |access-date=March 4, 2024 |work=The Independent}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Westwood |first=Katie |date=February 16, 2025 |title=Man claims to know truth about Elon Musk's Scouse nan |url=https://www.liverpoolecho.co.uk/news/liverpool-news/man-claims-know-truth-elon-31010424 |access-date=February 21, 2025 |work=Liverpool Echo}}</ref>

== Maye Musk ==
{{Main|Maye Musk}}
[[File:Maye-Musk.jpg|thumb|upright|Maye Musk in 2023]]

Maye Musk ({{née|Haldeman}}; born April{{nbsp}}19, 1948)<ref>{{Cite web |last=Musk |first=Maye |title=My 60th |url=http://mayemusk.blogspot.com/2010/01/feel-fantastic-at-60.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180621211414/http://mayemusk.blogspot.com/2010/01/feel-fantastic-at-60.html |archive-date=June 21, 2018 |access-date=December 12, 2016 |website=Maye Musk's Nutrition Blogs |publisher=[[Blogger (service)|Blogger]]}}</ref> is a model, [[dietitian]] and author.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Holson |first=Laura M. |date=April 30, 2016 |title=At 68, Maye Musk, the Mother of Elon, Is Reclaiming the Spotlight |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/01/fashion/elon-musk-mother-maye-musk-model-met-gala.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200628120358/https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/01/fashion/elon-musk-mother-maye-musk-model-met-gala.html |archive-date=June 28, 2020 |access-date=May 2, 2016 |website=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hou |first=Kathleen |last2=Musk |first2=Maye |date=March 17, 2016 |title=Elon Musk's Mom Is a 67-Year-Old Model and Dietitian with Great Wellness Advice |url=https://nymag.com/thecut/2016/03/maye-musk-elon-musk-model-interview.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170510164037/http://nymag.com/thecut/2016/03/maye-musk-elon-musk-model-interview.html |archive-date=May 10, 2017 |access-date=May 2, 2016 |website=[[New York (magazine)|New York]]}}</ref> She has been a model for 50 years, appearing on the covers of magazines, including a ''[[Time (magazine)|Time]]'' magazine health edition, [[Woman's Day|''Women's Day'']], international editions of [[Vogue (magazine)|''Vogue'']], and [[Sports Illustrated Swimsuit Issue|''Sports Illustrated'' Swimsuit Issue]]. She is the mother of [[Elon Musk]], [[Kimbal Musk]] and [[Tosca Musk]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Kay |first=Grace |date=February 4, 2023 |title=Meet Maye Musk, the glamorous model mother of billionaire Elon Musk |url=http://www.businessinsider.com/maye-musk-elon-musk-mother-model |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200620133410/https://www.businessinsider.com/maye-musk-elon-musk-mother-model |archive-date=June 20, 2020 |access-date=February 9, 2018 |work=[[Business Insider]] |language=en}}</ref> She holds Canadian, South African, and American citizenship. She is a registered dietitian. She published her memoir, ''A Woman Makes a Plan'' in 2019''.''

== Joshua Haldeman ==
{{Main|Joshua N. Haldeman}}
Haldeman was an American-born Canadian chiropractor and [[political activist]] who, in the early days of formalized [[apartheid]], moved to [[South Africa]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Sweet |first=Matthew |title=Why Jeff Bezos and Elon Musk's real business inspiration is science-fiction |url=https://www.thetimes.com/business-money/technology/article/why-jeff-bezos-and-elon-musks-real-business-inspiration-is-science-fiction-w805msw8t |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221214212250/https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/why-jeff-bezos-and-elon-musks-real-business-inspiration-is-science-fiction-w805msw8t |archive-date=December 14, 2022 |access-date=December 14, 2022 |work=[[The Times]] |language=en |issn=0140-0460}}</ref> Prior to the move, Haldeman headed the Canadian branch of [[Technocracy movement]] and ran for the [[Parliament of Canada]] on the [[Social Credit Party of Canada|Social Credit Party]] ticket.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Haldeman |first=Scott |last2=Keating Jr. |first2=Joseph C. |date=September 1995 |title=Joshua N Haldeman, DC: the Canadian Years, 1926-1950 |journal=The Journal of the Canadian Chiropractic Association |volume=39 |issue=3 |pages=172–186 |pmc=2485067}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Basen |first=Ira |title=In science we trust |url=https://newsinteractives.cbc.ca/longform/technocracy-incorporated-elon-musk/ |access-date=December 20, 2023 |website=[[CBC News]] |language=en}}</ref> Over the course of his life, he publicly expressed [[racist]], [[anti-Semitic]], and [[anti-democratic]] views, promoted a number of [[conspiracy theories]], and was a supporter of South Africa's [[apartheid]] system.<ref name="Benton-2023">{{Cite magazine |last=Benton |first=Joshua |author-link=Joshua Benton |date=September 21, 2023 |title=Elon Musk's Anti-Semitic, Apartheid-Loving Grandfather |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2023/09/joshua-haldeman-elon-musk-grandfather-apartheid-antisemitism/675396/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231007124423/https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2023/09/joshua-haldeman-elon-musk-grandfather-apartheid-antisemitism/675396/ |archive-date=October 7, 2023 |magazine=[[The Atlantic]]}}</ref>

The Haldeman couple spent time searching for the [[Lost City of the Kalahari]] by plane.<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 3, 2016 |title=Elon Musk's grandparents were adventuring pilots who spent years looking for a lost city in the desert |url=https://www.scmp.com/tech/tech-leaders-and-founders/article/1998521/elon-musks-grandparents-were-adventuring-pilots-who |access-date=September 6, 2023 |website=South China Morning Post |language=en}}</ref> Haldeman's mother Almeda Jane (Norman) Haldeman was the first recorded chiropractor in Canada.<ref name="Benton-2023"/>

== Wyn Fletcher ==
Winnifred Josephine Fletcher (1914–2012) was born in [[Moose Jaw]], Canada, to English parents. Her older sister Kay Fletcher married the Canadian [[ice hockey]] player [[Elmer Lach]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dowson |first=Richard |date=11 February 2024 |title=Researching Elon Musk's maternal grandmother born and raised in Moose Jaw |url=https://www.moosejawtoday.com/local-news/researching-elon-musks-maternal-grandmother-born-and-raised-in-moose-jaw-8281895 |website=Moose Jaw Today}}</ref>

According to her son-in-law Errol Musk, Wyn and her husband Joshua Haldeman were "fanatical" in favor of apartheid, and supported [[Nazism]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=McGreal |first1=Chris |title=How the roots of the ‘PayPal mafia’ extend to apartheid South Africa |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/26/elon-musk-peter-thiel-apartheid-south-africa |access-date=28 January 2025 |website=theguardian.com |publisher=The Guardian}}</ref> The grandmother of Elon Musk, she told Elon many stories of his grandfather's travels and exploits during his childhood, including slideshows of his trips.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Leo |first=Geoff |date=2025-03-20 |title=The Canadian roots of Elon Musk's conspiracist grandpa |url=https://www.cbc.ca/newsinteractives/features/joshua-haldeman-elon-musk-saskatchewan-tech-utopian-conspiracist |access-date=2025-05-16 |work=[[Canadian Broadcasting Corporation]]}}</ref>

== Walter Musk ==
Walter Henry James Musk was a South African World War II veteran.<ref>[https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/G9CJ-3LK/walter-henry-james-musk-1917-1986 Walter Musk's Military Record From WW2]</ref> He was from a mostly English-South African background.<ref name="Elon Musk's Liverpool Ancestors">[https://merseysidebiographypages.weebly.com/elon-musks-liverpool-ancestors.html Merseyside Biography Pages]</ref> According to family memory he served as a [[cryptographer]] in a [[military intelligence]] unit in Egypt during [[World War II]].{{sfn|Isaacson|2023|p=12}} He was the paternal grandfather of Elon Musk.

== Cora Robinson ==
Cora Amelia Robinson was born in [[Edge Hill, Liverpool]] to an English father and a South African mother. She moved to South Africa during World War II. Her father, from [[Toxteth]], [[Liverpool]], had emigrated to South Africa where he married her mother in 1911. Her mother was from a [[Afrikaner people|Dutch-South African]] background. They moved to [[Edge Hill, Liverpool]] and lived there until World War II.<ref name="Elon Musk's Liverpool Ancestors"/>

== Kimbal Musk ==
{{Main|Kimbal Musk}}
[[File:KIMBAL MUSK OFFICIAL HEADSHOT.jpg|thumb|upright|Kimbal Musk in 2013]]

Kimbal James Musk (born September{{nbsp}}20, 1972) is a South African [[restaurateur]], chef, and entrepreneur. He is the brother of [[Elon Musk]] and [[Tosca Musk]], and son of [[Errol Musk|Errol]] and [[Maye Musk]].

He owns The Kitchen Restaurant Group, a collection of restaurants located in [[Colorado]] and [[Chicago, Illinois|Chicago]].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Kimbal Reeve Musk to open restaurant on Mass Ave. |url=http://www.indystar.com/story/entertainment/2016/11/01/kimbal-musk-open-restaurant-mass-ave/93132032/ |access-date=July 31, 2017 |work=[[Indianapolis Star]] |language=en}}</ref> He is the co-founder and chairman of [[Big Green (non-profit company)|Big Green]], a [[501(c)(3) organization|501(c)(3) nonprofit]] that has built hundreds of outdoor classrooms called ''Learning Gardens'' in schoolyards across America.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Why every child deserves a learning garden |url=https://www.mnn.com/your-home/organic-farming-gardening/stories/why-every-child-deserves-learning-garden |access-date=July 31, 2017 |work=MNN - Mother Nature Network |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Padden |first=Caroline |date=October 29, 2012 |title=Learning Gardens: Connecting Kids to Real Food |url=http://www.5280.com/blogs/2012/10/29/learning-gardens-connecting-kids-real-food |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131111234216/http://www.5280.com/blogs/2012/10/29/learning-gardens-connecting-kids-real-food |archive-date=November 11, 2013 |access-date=June 6, 2013 |work=5280 Magazine}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Kimbal Musk — Elon's brother — is leading a $25 million mission to fix food in schools across the US |url=http://www.businessinsider.com/kimbal-musks-food-nonprofit-goes-national-learning-gardens-schools-2018-1 |access-date=January 17, 2018 |work=Business Insider |language=en}}</ref> Musk is also the co-founder and chairman of Square Roots, an urban farming company growing food in hydroponic, indoor, climate controlled shipping containers.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Lauren |first=Jennifer |date=January 27, 2017 |title=Kimbal Musk launches a revolutionary shipping container farm initiative in Brooklyn |url=http://inhabitat.com/nyc/kimbal-musk-just-launched-a-revolutionary-shipping-container-farm-initiative-in-brooklyn/ |work=[[Inhabitat Magazine]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Garfield |first=Leanna |date=August 23, 2016 |title=Elon Musk's brother is building vertical farms in shipping containers |url=http://www.businessinsider.com/kimbal-musk-vertical-farms-shipping-containers-2016-8 |work=Business Insider}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Scott |first=Bartie |date=August 23, 2016 |title=Elon Musk's Brother to Launch an Urban Farming Accelerator in Brooklyn |url=https://www.inc.com/bartie-scott/kimbal-musk-urban-farming-accelerator-square-roots.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180311051502/https://www.inc.com/bartie-scott/kimbal-musk-urban-farming-accelerator-square-roots.html |archive-date=March 11, 2018 |work=[[Inc Magazine]]}}</ref> Musk currently sits on the boards of [[Tesla Inc.]] and [[SpaceX]], both of which his brother Elon is the current CEO. He is a major shareholder in Tesla. He was on the board of [[Chipotle Mexican Grill]]<ref>{{Cite news |date=August 29, 2013 |title=Chipotle Mexican Grill names Kimbal Musk to board |url=http://www.denverpost.com/news/ci_23975683/chipotle-mexican-grill-names-kimbal-musk-board |work=Denver Post}}</ref> from 2013 to 2019.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Fitzgerald |first=Maggie |date=March 14, 2019 |title=Kimbal Musk is stepping down from Chipotle's board |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2019/03/14/kimbal-musk-is-stepping-down-from-chipotles-board.html |access-date=April 10, 2019 |website=[[CNBC]]}}</ref>

In 1995 he co-founded, with his brother, Elon Musk, the software company [[Zip2]], which was acquired by [[Compaq]] for $307 million in 1999.

Kimbal Musk was married to [[Jen Lewin]], with whom he established The Kitchen, from 2001 to 2010. The couple had two children together.<ref>{{Cite news |date=June 29, 2015 |title=Husted: Kimbal Musk, restaurateur and brother of rocketman Elon Musk (Slideshow) |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/denver/blog/Broadway_17th/2015/06/husted-kimbal-musk-restaurateur-and-brother-of.html |access-date=June 29, 2017 |work=Bizjournals}}</ref> In April 2018, he married Christiana Wyly, an environmental activist and the daughter of ex-billionaire [[Sam Wyly]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Gubbins |first=Teresa |date=April 9, 2018 |title=Kimbal Musk and Wyly heiress celebrate wedding at Dallas restaurant |url=http://dallas.culturemap.com/news/restaurants-bars/04-09-18-cedar-social-wedding-reception-kimbal-musk-christiana-wyly/ |access-date=April 9, 2018 |work=CultureMap}}</ref>

Musk also has a daughter from another relationship.<ref>{{Cite web |date=17 September 2018 |title=A Tale of Two Kitchens |url=https://www.coloradohomesmag.com/a-tale-of-two-kitchens/}}</ref> One of his children is [[transgender]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-02-14 |title=Errol Musk Says Son Elon 'Hasn't Been a Good Father' in Wild Interview |url=https://www.thedailybeast.com/errol-musk-says-son-elon-hasnt-been-a-good-father-in-wild-interview/ |access-date=2025-02-15 |website=The Daily Beast |language=en}}</ref>

== Tosca Musk ==
{{Main|Tosca Musk}}
[[File:Tosca-Musk Founder-CEO Passionflix March 1 2019.jpg|thumb|upright|Tosca Musk in 2019]]

Tosca Musk (born July{{nbsp}}20, 1974) is a South African filmmaker, who is the younger sister of [[Elon Musk]] and [[Kimbal Musk]], and daughter of [[Errol Musk]] and [[Maye Musk]].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Model Maye Musk On Defying The Odds And Her Influence On Elon |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/moiraforbes/2018/10/04/model-maye-musk-on-defying-the-odds-and-her-influence-on-elon/#4c6249ca2c02 |work=forbes.com}}</ref>

She is an executive producer and director of feature films, television programs, and web content. Her work includes K. Bromberg's ''Driven'', Rachel van Dyken's ''Matchmaker's Playbook'', and her web series, ''[[Tiki Bar TV]]''.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Meet Elon Musk's Rather Impressive Family |url=http://www.2oceansvibe.com/2018/10/03/meet-elon-musks-rather-impressive-family/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221027154305/https://www.2oceansvibe.com/2018/10/03/meet-elon-musks-rather-impressive-family/ |archive-date=October 27, 2022 |access-date=August 9, 2024 |work=2oceansvibe.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Kee |first=Tameka |date=May 19, 2009 |title=paidContent.org - Tiki Bar TV Tests The Pay-To-Watch Webisode Model |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/content/article/2009/05/18/AR2009051802626.html |work=The Washington Post}}</ref> She co-founded the movie-streaming service [[Passionflix]].<ref name=":02">{{Cite news |last=Keegan |first=Rebecca |date=February 13, 2025 |title=Elon Musk’s Sister Is a Hopeless Romantic |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/elon-musk-sister-tosca-musk-passionflix-1236133590/ |access-date=April 28, 2025 |work=The Hollywood Reporter}}</ref><ref name=":1">{{Cite news |last=Stephan |first=Katcy |date=December 20, 2024 |title=How Tosca Musk Crafted Passionflix, the World’s Steamiest Niche Streaming Service |url=https://variety.com/2024/film/news/passionflix-tosca-musk-streamer-1236256897/ |access-date=April 28, 2025 |work=Variety}}</ref>

