== Lyndon Rive ==
{{Main|Lyndon Rive}}
[[File:Lyndon Rive 2015.jpg|thumb|upright|Lyndon Rive in 2015]]

Lyndon Robert Rive (born 22{{nbsp}}January 1977) is a South African-American businessman known as the co-founder of [[SolarCity]], and its [[Chief executive officer|CEO]] until 2016. SolarCity is a provider of [[photovoltaic]] systems and related services. Rive co-founded SolarCity with his brother Peter in 2006. He is a cousin of Elon Musk; his mother Kaye Rive is the twin sister of Maye Musk.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Aman Jain |date=2020-02-01 |title=Lyndon Rive, Elon Musk's Cousin And Former SolarCity CEO To Exit Tesla |url=https://www.valuewalk.com/rive-musk-cousin-solarcity-exit-tesla/ |access-date=2025-02-08}}</ref>

Rive started his first company at age 17 before leaving his native country, South Africa.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hansen |first=Louis |date=2015-12-11 |title=Q&A: SolarCity CEO Lyndon Rive keeps business all in the family |url=https://www.mercurynews.com/2015/12/11/qa-solarcity-ceo-lyndon-rive-keeps-business-all-in-the-family/ |access-date=2021-04-27 |website=The Mercury News |language=en-US}}</ref> He then co-founded the enterprise software company [[Everdream]], which was ultimately acquired by [[Dell]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Milo |first=Moryt |date=28 December 2010 |title=Lyndon Rive, Elon Musk: Cousins, partners |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/sanjose/blog/2010/12/family-joins-colleagues-for-teslas-musk.html |access-date=2021-04-27 |website=bizjournals.com}}</ref> In 2010, Rive was named in the [[Technology Review|''MIT Technology Review's'']] [[Innovators Under 35]] as one of the top 35 innovators in the world under the age of 35.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2010 |title=2010: Innovators Under 35 |url=http://www2.technologyreview.com/tr35/profile.aspx?trid=970 |access-date=1 November 2018 |work=MIT Technology Review}}</ref>

Rive's parents were entrepreneurs in the natural-health business in [[Pretoria]], South Africa. Rive has three siblings: SolarCity co-founder Peter Rive, Russ Rive who runs an art, technology, and design company in Brazil, and competitive [[dirt bike]] rider {{interlanguage link|Almeda Rive|de}}.<ref>{{Cite magazine |date=2015-10-21 |title=How Elon Musk's Mom (and her Twin Sister) Raised the First Family of Tech |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2015/10/elon-musk-family-maye-musk |access-date=2023-11-18 |magazine=Vanity Fair |language=en-US}}</ref>
